    "summary": "Wrapper composed of sixth lengths of hand plain woven narrow strip lengths and a single machine woven length hand sewn together selvedge to selvedge. The narrow strips are composed of dyed indigo warps and wefts and dyed light blue wefts creating light blue cotton warp stripes running the full length of the wrapper. The wrapper consists of a single machine woven bleached white length embroidered  with a repeating geometric pattern in dyed brown cotton which is flanked by three widths of narrow strip woven cotton. The warp ends are lined with printed fabric.",
